# What `docker build` never needs, kept out of its build context. On a build node the context is the project folder deploy.sh
# unpacked, and deploy.sh moves the node's data/ and .env back into it before `docker compose up --build`, so without this file
# the ledger, community.key and the node's secrets went to the builder (scratch/reviews/FABLE-sec-infra.md M1). The image never
# held them (its runtime stage copies named paths), but the builder's cache did until the prune at the end of a deploy.
# A pattern matches from the context root; **/ matches at any depth. scripts/test-deploy-package.sh checks these lines.

# The node's own data and secrets.
data
**/.env*

# Working state in a developer's checkout, should a build run from one.
.claude
scratch*
.deploy-package.tar.gz

# What the build installs or makes for itself.
.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo

# The phone app and its build output. The node image never uses apps/native, and deploy.sh has never sent it to a build node.
apps/native
builds
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
